      <span class="release-tab-meta">iPhone 1.1.0 (124)</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <article class="release-panel is-active" id="desktop" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="release-tab-desktop" tabindex="0">
    <div class="release-panel-head">
      <p class="release-platform">Desktop</p>
      <h2>Cueport 1.1.0 for macOS</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="release-panel-grid">
      <div>
        <h3>What changed</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Read Serato crates, subcrates, tracks, cues, BPM, key, color, comments, and beatgrid markers from your local library.</li>
          <li>Try Cueport Direct as an experimental local library built from music folders, with local BPM, key, waveform, and color analysis from trail mix.</li>
          <li>Play tracks on desktop with waveform context, cue markers, skip controls, and continuous playback.</li>
          <li>Create, rename, delete, add tracks to, and manually reorder collections before publishing changes back.</li>
          <li>Use automatic restore points before Serato write-back and Cueport Direct changes.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Build details</h3>
        <dl class="release-facts">
          <div>
            <dt>Analysis engine</dt>
            <dd><a href="https://github.com/djpardis/trailmix/commit/ea86514c70e678148969533704768b9ae43b6b56">trail mix paper-preview 2026-11-07 (ea86514c)</a></dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Cueport Direct</dt>
            <dd>Experimental in this release.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
